{
  "about": "What a user can do, and how each client reaches it. Every API route is a capability here or listed in internalRoutes; each surface names its calls (SDK methods, CLI commands, MCP tools), or says in a sentence why it has none, and mcpHosted says when the hosted MCP server lacks a tool the local one has. A capability counts as covered when its calls reach its routes; split one when a client reaches only some of them. Nobody should need the dashboard: a capability every client lacks is a gap to close, sessionOnly says why a person still has to be in the loop, and approval says what a person approves when an API key or agent asks (the route answers 202 with an approval). Checked by packages/sdk/src/__tests__/capabilities.test.ts, packages/mcp/src/__tests__/capabilities.test.ts and apps/cli-rs (cli::capabilities).",
